{number: 93}
{title: He Leadeth Me! O Blessed Tho’t}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D] He leadeth me! O [G] blessed thought!
O [D] words with heav'nly [A7] comfort fraught!
What-[D] e'er I do, wher-[G] e'er I be,
Still [D] 'tis God's hand that [A7] leadeth [D] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
He [D] leadeth me, He [G] leadeth me,
By [D] His own hand He [A7] leadeth me:
His [D] faithful foll'wer [G] I would be,
For [D] by His hand He [A7] leadeth [D] me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Some-[D] times 'mid scenes of [G] deepest gloom,
Some-[D] times where Eden's [A7] bowers bloom,
By [D] waters still, o'er [G] troubled sea,
Still [D] 'tis His hand that [A7] leadeth [D] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Lord, [D] I would clasp Thy [G] hand in mine,
Nor [D] ever murmur [A7] nor repine;
Con-[D] tent, whatever [G] lot I see,
Since [D] 'tis my God that [A7] leadeth [D] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
And [D] when my task on [G] earth is done,
When, [D] by Thy grace, the [A7] vict'ry's won,
E'en [D] death's cold wave I [G] will not flee,
Since [D] God through Jordan [A7] leadeth [D] me.
{end_of_verse}
